# Moves/DefsL — the round-5 (FINAL) localization objects for the MOVES tower induction (§B2-DEF)

**Provenance.** `lean/notes/MOVES_2026-07-24.md` §B2-DEF (D.0–D.11). ROUND-5 design layer,
answering the four demands of audit #4 (`lean/notes/MOVES_LEAN_SEMAUDIT4_2026-07-26.md`).
Imports `Defs.lean`/`DefsT.lean`/`DefsCore.lean` UNCHANGED. Design rationale and the per-demand
(a)/(b) record: blueprint `MOVES_LEAN_BLUEPRINT_2026-07-26.md` § ROUND 5. Definitions plus two
two-line lemmas (`locT` unit equations, `grRes_mul_T_neg` — the definitional normalization);
no `sorry`, no axioms.

## The round-5 design: the graded localization, built concretely as `L = L₀[T^{±1}]`

D.1(e) — proved once in the accepted §B2-DEF — says the localization `L = 𝒢[⟨U ∪ {Y}⟩⁻¹]` of a
stage with degree-1 unit `T` is CANONICALLY `L₀[T^{±1}]`, via `x ↦ R(x)·T^{deg x}` on homogeneous
elements. Under the standing round-1 codomain fiat (`L₀ := LaurentPolynomial ↥σ.K` — the D2 flag,
carried unchanged), that canonical presentation is a CONCRETE ring:

  `LTwo ↥σ.K := LaurentPolynomial (LaurentPolynomial ↥σ.K)`   (inner variable `z`, outer `T`),

and the initial-form map is `Stage.grRes f := C (σ.R f) · T (σ.w f)` — so `T` (the outer
variable, the unit `locT`) IS an actual localized element, and the normalization
`R(f) = [f]·T^{−w(f)}` holds definitionally (`grRes_mul_T_neg`). The StageCore tie laws
(`w_strict`/`w_jump`/`R_neg`, round 4) make `grRes` injective on graded classes, so identities
of `grRes`-images are equivalent to identities of genuine initial forms in any genuine model:
the constructions below state the D.0(P2)/D.2(S4)/D.7(vi)/D.8 laws about ACTUAL objects.

* **Demand 1 (T-vector → actual localized normalizing unit): `TvecUnitLaw`** — the product
  identity `Π in(ũᵢ)^{aᵢ} · Y^t = T` as an equation between UNITS of `LTwo`, factors pinned to
  `grRes` of the literal `σ.Tvec` entries (whose support IS `σ.reps`, by `Stage.hTvec`) and the
  key; exponents the literal vector entries. Replaces the two-evaluation shadow `TvecLaw`
  (propositionally equivalent under the Stage laws — but now stated at the locus D.0(P2)
  specifies, with `T` present as the element the law is about).
* **Demand 2 (S4 = the coefficient LOCALIZATION): `Stage.coeffLocSR` + `CoeffLocLaw`** — the
  coefficient localization `𝒞[⟨U⟩⁻¹]` as a genuine `Subring (LTwo ↥σ.K)` (generated by the
  coefficient initial forms and the INVERSES of the representative units), with (S4) stated of
  it: degree-0 part = `K` exactly (both inclusions), plus the (P1) pinning — `z` realized
  EXACTLY (scalar 1) as a degree-0 formal `U ∪ {Y}`-monomial vector (`IsLVecVal`, exponent
  vectors over the genuine representative list). Rank-1-ness of the exponent group is no longer
  imposed by the codomain alone: graded injectivity (tie laws) transfers it to any genuine model.
* **Demand 3 (D.8 transport on Laurent slot terms + terminal carry): `IsCarryChainL` /
  `CarryTransportL` / `LandingCylinderL`** — the triangular recursion as a RELATIONAL chain on
  LAURENT slot terms `c_j = T(j·m̂ − a)·R(B_j)` (no polynomial coercion: negative `z`-powers may
  cancel only across ψ-levels, exactly as D.8 displays), digits the canonical `deg < g`
  representatives, carries Laurent, and the terminal no-overflow `carry j = 0` for `j ≥ N`
  RECORDED as a clause. The chain's witness is unique (deterministic both ways on actual loci —
  the D.8 triangular bijection); the executable `carryRec` of round 4 is retired from the
  cylinder.
* **Demand 4 (P6i scalar action preserves the piece)** — no new object: the corrected `L2.P6i`
  statement (MANIFEST_FINAL) hypothesizes `σ.w û = 0` and concludes `σ.w (û·f) = γ` with the
  scaling — an endomorphism of the fixed graded piece.
* **`StageCoreL` / `TransitionCoreL`** — the round-4 cores extended by the new laws; the
  transition record `child_dig_frame` now carries the frame-unit exponent as a function of the
  PARENT WEIGHT alone (`∃ mfun : ℤ → ℤ` BEFORE `∀ B`) — the per-index coherence `TRANSviii_a`'s
  `∃ m, ∀ c` needs (audit #4's uniform-orbit demand).

All items are flagged for semantic-guardian review (the trust boundary). The single remaining
boundary — the identification of `(σ.R, σ.w)` with the residual calculus of a genuine graded
tower (the round-1 D2 fiat + D.1(e)) — is restated, unchanged, in blueprint § ROUND 5 with the
full spec of the graded-ring campaign that would discharge it.
-/

